---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Accessibility statement';
const description = 'The accessibility target, current testing status, known limitations and contact routes for OPDA public services.';
---
<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  hideSidebar
  hideBreadcrumbs
  hideFooter
  hideComments
  wrapArticle={false}
  suppressActiveDestination
>
  <article class="public-statement" aria-labelledby="accessibility-title">
    <header class="public-statement__header">
      <p class="public-statement__eyebrow">Open Property Data Association</p>
      <h1 id="accessibility-title">Accessibility statement</h1>
      <p class="public-statement__lead">
        We want the OPDA public website to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines
        version 2.2 at Level AA.
      </p>
      <p class="public-statement__meta">
        <span>Prepared 27 August 2026</span>
        <span>Last reviewed 3 September 2026</span>
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="public-statement__content" aria-labelledby="scope-title">
      <h2 id="scope-title">What this statement covers</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          This statement covers the public <a href="/join">working-group service</a> and its
          <a href="/join/privacy">privacy notice</a>, the <a href="/subscribe">newsletter
          subscription service</a> and its <a href="/subscribe/privacy">privacy notice</a>, and
          this accessibility page. It does not cover every page in the OPDA Knowledge Base.
        </p>
        <p>
          WCAG 2.2 Level AA is the standard we are working towards. We do not claim that every
          covered page currently meets it, and these pages have not been independently certified
          as conformant.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-statement__content" aria-labelledby="use-title">
      <h2 id="use-title">Using the service</h2>
      <div>
        <p>We design the covered pages so people can:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>navigate and complete the registration form with a keyboard;</li>
          <li>zoom and reflow content without losing information or controls;</li>
          <li>use text alternatives and semantic HTML when visual diagrams are present;</li>
          <li>read content with sufficient colour contrast and without relying on colour alone; and</li>
          <li>disable non-essential motion through their device preferences.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-statement__content" aria-labelledby="testing-title">
      <h2 id="testing-title">How we assess accessibility</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          Our release checks cover code-level accessibility assertions, keyboard use, colour
          contrast, reduced motion, forced colours, and reflow at 320 CSS pixels and 400% zoom.
          Automated checks find only some accessibility problems and do not prove full WCAG
          conformance.
        </p>
        <p>
          We have not yet completed a full manual or independent accessibility audit of these
          pages. Additional issues may exist. We will update this statement with the tested build,
          routes, browsers, assistive technologies, tools and findings when that audit is complete.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-statement__content" aria-labelledby="limitations-title">
      <h2 id="limitations-title">Known limitations</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          The working-group registration and newsletter subscription journeys have not yet had a
          full manual audit with assistive technology. Their content and controls use ordinary
          semantic HTML and do not depend on motion or an interactive visual, but further issues
          may still be found.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because the broader Knowledge Base is outside the current testing scope, this statement
          does not make a conformance claim for generated ontology documentation, diagrams or
          historic material elsewhere on the site.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-statement__content" aria-labelledby="formats-title">
      <h2 id="formats-title">Alternative formats and support</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          If you need information from these pages in another format, or need help using the
          working-group registration or newsletter subscription service, email
          <a href="mailto:smartdata@openpropdata.org.uk">smartdata@openpropdata.org.uk</a>.
          Tell us which page or information you need and the format or support that would help.
        </p>
        <p>
          Do not include confidential, customer, property-transaction or special-category
          information in your email.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-statement__content" aria-labelledby="report-title">
      <h2 id="report-title">Report a problem</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          To report a problem, email
          <a href="mailto:smartdata@openpropdata.org.uk">smartdata@openpropdata.org.uk</a> and tell
          us which page you were on, what you were trying to do and what went wrong. If you are
          comfortable doing so, also tell us your browser, device and any assistive technology
          you use.
        </p>
        <p>
          Open Property Data Association Ltd is responsible for this statement and the covered
          public working-group service.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
